  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer array AAA of size NNN and a positive integer MMM. This array contains a hidden message which can be decoded by the following algorithm:\n\n`int ox[N+1], oy[N+1];\nfor(int i = 1; i ≤ N; i++) {\n    ox[i] = A[i] / M;\n    oy[i] = A[i] % M;\n}\n`There are NNN landmines on the xy-plane, such that the ithi^{th}ith landmine (1≤i≤N)(1\\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N) is located at (oxi,oyi)(ox_i,oy_i)(oxi​,oyi​).\n\nInitially, you are at point (0,0)(0,0)(0,0) and you must go to point (X,Y)(X,Y)(X,Y). At each step, you can either move to the right by 111 unit or move up by 111 unit.\n\nFormally, if you are standing at (x,y)(x,y)(x,y), then you can either move to (x+1,y)(x+1,y)(x+1,y) or to (x,y+1)(x,y+1)(x,y+1).\n\nA path is called safe if there aren't any landmines on that path. Count the number of safe paths which you can take to reach the destination. As the answer can be quite large, output it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains 444 integers NNN, MMM, XXX, and YYY where (X,Y)(X,Y)(X,Y) are the coordinates of your destination on the xy-plane.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ representing the initial array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput, in a single line, the number of safe paths modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤M≤1061 \\leq M \\leq 10^61≤M≤106",
      "0≤X,Y≤1060 \\leq X, Y \\leq 10^60≤X,Y≤106",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^61≤Ai​≤106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 4 2 3\n5 6 5",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor the given array A=[5,6,5]A = [5, 6, 5]A=[5,6,5], the location of the landmines are given by ox=[54,64,54]=[1,1,1]ox = [\\frac{5}{4}, \\frac{6}{4}, \\frac{5}{4}] = [1, 1, 1]ox=[45​,46​,45​]=[1,1,1] and oy=[5%4,6%4,5%4]=[1,2,1]oy = [5\\%4, 6\\%4, 5\\%4] = [1, 2, 1]oy=[5%4,6%4,5%4]=[1,2,1]. Thus, landmines are at (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) and (1,2)(1,2)(1,2).\nThere are 222 safe paths to reach the destination. The safe paths are highlighted in the figure bellow:"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 3 3 3\n4 8",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nLandmines are located at (1,1)(1, 1)(1,1) and (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2)."
      }
    ]
  },
